  "title": "Islands keep the count hard",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Islands keep the count hard. Restrict the knot-sphere formula of K_k by any island packing: balls of radius s, pairwise at distance at least 17 and away from the corners, each fixed to one constant label in a frame over the island. The restricted formula still needs resolution width at least c(s)*k - 1. With the island points as permanent pebbles in the window criterion, terms within an island are nonnegative and terms between islands are at least floor((dist - 11)/6), hence >= 1; so every negative term of an obstruction certificate touches a Spoiler pebble, the certificate walk has length O(s^3) per Spoiler pebble, and the density argument of SPHERE-WIDTH-20261107-001A goes through with the vortex in the free region.",
